    Requirement('SR-063', 'FR-PAY-02', 'M', 'C', '§5', 'Salary structure: {emp_id, basic, hra, allowances[], deductions[], effective_from}; multiple structures per employee are allowed with non-overlapping effective ranges (exclusion constraint). Preview endpoint uses the exact same calculation function as the payroll run (FR-PAY-05) — one function, not two (Appendix A-07).'),
    Requirement('SR-064', 'FR-PAY-03', 'M', 'C', '§5', 'Payroll rates (PF/ESI/PT/TDS) are versioned, effective-dated configuration, editable by Finance, fully audited; a run always uses the rates effective on the run’s period end date.'),
    Requirement('SR-065', 'FR-PAY-04', 'M', 'C', '§5', 'Calculation: gross = basic + hra + Σallowances; pf = min(gross × pf_rate, pf_max); esi = gross × esi_rate if gross ≤ esi_max else 0; pt = pt_amount if gross > pt_threshold else 0; TDS per the configured slab table (not hard-coded percentages); LOP is deducted using FR-LEA-09’s working-day function against the days marked Absent/Half-day by FR-JOB-01; approved, unpaid reimbursements for the period are added to net pay. net = gross − (Σdeductions + pf + esi + pt + tds) − lop_amount + reimbursements. All amounts NUMERIC(14,2).'),
    Requirement('SR-066', 'FR-PAY-05', 'M', 'C', '§5', "Run POST /api/payroll-runs {month, year}: duplicate (month, year, status != 'Cancelled') prevented by a unique constraint; executes as a background job covering every employee with status Active or Onboarding whose salary structure is effective for the period (v1.0 covered only role = Employee, silently excluding managers and HR — Appendix A-08); created in status Draft; progress is pollable."),
    Requirement('SR-067', 'FR-PAY-06', 'H', 'N', '§5', 'Maker-checker approval. Draft → Submitted (Finance) → Approved (a different Finance/Admin user) → Finalized. A run cannot be approved by the user who submitted it. Once Finalized, payroll items are immutable; corrections require a new run (an adjustment run) referencing the original. v1.0 had no approval step (Appendix A-09).'),
