    Requirement('SR-096', 'FR-ATS-02', 'M', 'C', '§5', 'Jobs and candidates CRUD (HR/Admin); candidate status change via the same stage machine (no arbitrary jump to Hired).'),
    Requirement('SR-097', 'FR-ATS-03', 'M', 'C', '§5', 'Convert-to-employee is not a manual action — it is a consequence of POST /api/offers/<id>/accept (FR-ATS-04). A candidate reaches Hired only through an accepted offer, closing the v1.0 gap where a candidate could be marked Hired directly without ever having an offer (Appendix A-19).'),
    Requirement('SR-098', 'FR-ATS-04', 'M', 'C', '§5', 'Offers: {candidate_id, offered_salary, basic_pct, hra_pct, allowances_pct} where the three percentages sum to 100 (validated) — v1.0’s fixed 50/20/20 split silently discarded 10% of salary (Appendix A-20). Accept → candidate Hired, creates the salary structure and (via a domain event) triggers onboarding checklist creation (FR-ONB-03). Reject/Accept on a missing or already-decided offer returns 404/409, not a silent no-op (v1.0’s idempotent-but-wrong 200 — Appendix A-21).'),
    Requirement('SR-099', 'FR-JOB-01', 'M', 'N', '§5', 'Daily attendance finalisation, nightly per shift date: for every active employee, classify the day as Present, Half-day, Absent, On Leave, Holiday or Weekly-off, from sessions, approved leave, holidays and the employee’s weekly-off pattern (not a hard-coded Mon–Fri — Appendix A-22). Written to attendance_days, the single source for reports and payroll LOP. Idempotent: re-running for a date replaces that date’s rows in one transaction.'),
